      "kind": "summary",
      "id": "executive-summary",
      "title": "Executive summary",
      "text": "Exercise Tidal Moon is a rehearsal tabletop exercise designed for national CERT leaders in the ASEAN region. Set during the 2026 holiday season, the scenario involves a regional cyber incident causing intermittent cross-border QR payment failures. Participants must work together to assess the incident's impact, cause, and severity, while navigating various information streams, including a potential red herring involving monsoon-related telecommunications issues. The primary goal is to achieve regional consensus on a coordinated response and public communication strategy. The exercise is designed to be discussion-based, focusing on decision-making and cooperation rather than technical tasks.",
      "visibility": "participant",
      "standing": "stated"
    }
